ARM GAS  /var/folders/8x/_y6g3dfs0698dfd49y4vcg_w0000gn/T//ccowXl7k.s 			page 19


 973:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_i2c.c ****  *  @brief   Data transfers functions
 974:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_i2c.c ****  *
 975:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_i2c.c **** @verbatim
 976:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_i2c.c ****  ===============================================================================
 977:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_i2c.c ****                       ##### IO operation functions #####
 978:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_i2c.c ****  ===============================================================================
 979:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_i2c.c ****     [..]
 980:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_i2c.c ****     This subsection provides a set of functions allowing to manage the I2C data
 981:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_i2c.c ****     transfers.
 982:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_i2c.c **** 
 983:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_i2c.c ****     (#) There are two modes of transfer:
 984:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (++) Blocking mode : The communication is performed in the polling mode.
 985:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_i2c.c ****             The status of all data processing is returned by the same function
 986:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_i2c.c ****             after finishing transfer.
 987:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (++) No-Blocking mode : The communication is performed using Interrupts
 988:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_i2c.c ****             or DMA. These functions return the status of the transfer startup.
 989:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_i2c.c ****             The end of the data processing will be indicated through the
 990:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_i2c.c ****             dedicated I2C IRQ when using Interrupt mode or the DMA IRQ when
 991:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_i2c.c ****             using DMA mode.
